{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after creating a website called facemash, which compares the photos of two students and asks users to vote on which one is more attractive, zuckerberg gains notoriety and catches the attention of the winklevoss twins, who approach him with an idea for a social networking site.\n\nzuckerberg agrees to work on the site, but eventually drops the project and starts working on his own site, thefacebook, with his friends eduardo saverin and andrew mccollum. the site quickly gains popularity, and zuckerberg becomes a celebrity on campus. however, the winklevoss twins claim that zuckerberg stole their idea, and they file a lawsuit against him.\n\nthe movie follows the story of the lawsuit, as well as the story of zuckerberg's relationships with his friends and family. the film is well-acted, with eisenberg giving a standout performance as zuckerberg. the supporting cast, including andrew garfield as saverin and justin timberlake as sean parker, is also excellent.\n\nthe film's script, written by aaron sorkin, is witty and engaging, and the dialogue is often humorous and insightful. the movie's direction, by david fincher, is also noteworthy, with a dark and moody tone that reflects the complexity and intensity of the story.\n\none of the most interesting aspects of the movie is its portrayal of the characters and their motivations. zuckerberg is depicted as a complex and multifaceted person, who is both brilliant and awkward. the film also explores the themes of friendship, loyalty, and the consequences of success.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-made and engaging film that tells a fascinating story. the movie's themes and characters are well-developed, and the acting and direction are excellent. the film is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028232974000275135}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.10020723193883896}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.008624685928225517}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.18487101793289185}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0005295066512189806}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.39684411883354187}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00977491494268179}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.014305301010608673}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00012265883560758084}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.575939416885376}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.18180598318576813}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.970903682988137e-05}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.20398323237895966}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.6422874927520752}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00048792376765049994}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0004297763225622475}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -4.2199197196168825e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0006291079334914684}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -8.34461570775602e-06}, {"token": " begins", "logprob": -0.7941714525222778}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -7.60526381782256e-05}, {"token": " mark", "logprob": -1.3112935448589269e-05}, {"token": " z", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": "ucker", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": "berg", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " played", "logprob": -0.004166375380009413}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -9.298280929215252e-0